Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: git-purge-branches
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, git (>= 1:2.41)
Description: delete local branches merged into a commit
 git purge-branches deletes the local branches merged into a commit, HEAD by
 default, except those checked out in any worktree and those exempt through
 branch.<name>.deleteMerged. With --equivalent, it also deletes branches that
 a remote rebased before merging.
